= April 2026 — Association before ultimatum

Former prime minister <span class="party-pis"><b>Mateusz Morawiecki</b></span>, still a PiS politician, opens the
first Rozwój+ convention under banners promising investment, technology and a
less punitive conservatism. PiS parliamentarians and former ministers
<span class="party-pis"><b>Olga Semeniuk-Patkowska</b></span>, <span class="party-pis"><b>Janusz Cieszyński</b></span> and <span class="party-pis"><b>Paweł Jabłoński</b></span> appear
on its organising lists. They retain their PiS membership and mandates.

Rozwój+ now has members, local activity and an internal programme. It is **not
a Sejm club and not a political party**. <span class="party-pis"><b>Jarosław Kaczyński</b></span>, PiS chair,
tolerates a current that still asks his permission to remain inside the
caucus; Morawiecki is building the ability to survive the day that permission
ends.

[? if government_party = "pis" and left_in_government: Lewica sits in a
PiS-led cabinet while its senior partner divides. A dialogue can stabilise the
government, an attack can hurry the rupture, and a policy concession can make
Morawiecki stronger without moving a single seat.?][? if government_party !=
"pis" or not left_in_government: For Lewica this is a rival organisation inside
a rival party. It may keep both PiS camps talking, test the new brand against
Morawiecki's record or give his current an issue victory inside PiS.?]

- @rozwoj_association_alliance
- @rozwoj_association_attack
- @rozwoj_association_social

@rozwoj_association_alliance
