= [+ date_label +] — A new anti-system market right

**[+ p0_name +]** has stopped being a broadcast and started being an
organisation. **Krzysztof Stanowski's** project files committee papers, opens
regional offices and appears in three consecutive polls above the noise, and
the people it is taking are not one party's.

Our own regional secretaries report the same thing from opposite ends of the
country: young men who voted Konfederacja, small employers who voted PiS, and a
thinner but real slice of urban professionals who voted KO and have decided
that all of it is theatre. No bloc gets to treat this as somebody else's
defection.

[? if p0_peak = 3: The established right is already moving to close the gap,
and the likeliest version of this is a loud insurgency that stalls in the low
single figures once PiS remembers how to talk to its own base.?]
[? if p0_peak = 6: Nothing about its support looks like a summer enthusiasm.
On present trends it settles as a permanent second force on the right — not
large enough to govern, large enough to decide who does.?]
[? if p0_peak = 11: The numbers are not a protest vote. If they hold, [+
p0_short_name +] does not join the right's arithmetic; it replaces a good part
of it, and every existing machine on that side is playing for survival.?]

Two things follow for us. The radical right's argument has acquired a fluent,
media-native vehicle that no cordon reaches. And every democratic rival will now
be tempted to chase it with harder borders and lower taxes, which is how a
party with three percent sets the agenda for parties with thirty.

- @p0_response_isolate_2026
- @p0_response_material_2026
- @p0_response_alarm_2026

@p0_response_isolate_2026
title: Isolate the party as a media vehicle, not a programme
subtitle: Deny it anti-system glamour and force specific policy comparisons.
on-arrival: media_capacity += 2; public_trust += 1; p0_poll_momentum -= 0.12; p0_ai_actions -= 1 if p0_ai_actions > 0; news_headline = "Lewica treats Partia Zero as a media vehicle rather than a governing offer"

Lewica spokespeople stop answering clips and start answering costings: who
pays, which statute changes, which office is supposed to enforce it. Asked in
that register, a media insurgency has to produce a spokesman who has read a
budget.

It works and it is exhausting. The discipline has to hold every week, on every
programme, including the ones where the obvious reply would travel further, and
one undisciplined evening returns the argument to their ground.

- @poland_event_queue: Change the register

@p0_response_material_2026
title: Re-anchor the campaign in wages, rents and services
subtitle: Accept that cultural escalation feeds P0; move the fight to material security.
on-arrival: labor_credibility += 3; workers_support += 2; household_policy_pressure += 4; left_poll_momentum += 0.10; p0_poll_momentum -= 0.06; news_headline = "Lewica answers Partia Zero with a material-security campaign"

We stop contesting the cultural argument, on the grounds that it is the one
they win, and take the campaign back to rents, fares and the price of a weekly
shop. Anti-system anger does not disappear; it stops automatically finding its
way to a party whose economic programme is a tax cut.

The cost is visible immediately in the places where the cultural fight is the
one our own members wanted. We have conceded a field to buy a smaller, firmer
one.

- @poland_event_queue: Take the campaign back to rents

@p0_response_alarm_2026
title: Declare P0 an immediate democratic danger
subtitle: Mobilise the anti-far-right base quickly, at the cost of broad persuasion.
on-arrival: progressive_credibility += 3; media_capacity += 1; p0_poll_momentum += 0.08; konf_poll_momentum += 0.05; public_trust -= 1; news_headline = "An emergency anti-P0 line hardens both camps"

We name it as a democratic danger and the base responds within the day —
petitions, meetings, the organisations that mobilised against Braun turning out
again with three years of practice behind them.

Stanowski could not have written a better week for himself. The persecution he
has been describing arrives with our signature on it, and right-wing voters who
found him ridiculous discover they resent us more. We have activated our people
and recruited his.

- @poland_event_queue: Issue the warning

@partnership_passes_2026
