Lewica trains local legal-aid desks to follow the first registrations, hospital
disputes and inheritance cases. [? if left_in_government and
equality_minister_party = "Lewica": Equality Minister **[+ equality_minister
+]** receives the reports and carries them to the competent registry, health
and justice offices before their implementation orders are due.?][? if
left_in_government and equality_minister_party != "Lewica": The desks send
their reports to the serving Equality Ministry and the responsible offices.
Lewica can press those ministers in cabinet; it cannot turn Kotula's party role
into authority over their departments.?][? if not left_in_government: The
network cannot direct the cabinet, but it can expose every office that treats a
signed law as optional.?] A signature becomes something couples can test in a
real room, not a triumph left on the Sejm board.

- @poland_event_queue: Train the legal-aid desks

@partnership_signed_expand
title: Treat signature as the bridge to marriage equality
subtitle: Celebrate the protection, then ask Parliament why legal partnership should remain the ceiling.
view-if: partnership_presidential_outcome = "Signed"
on-arrival: progressive_credibility += 5; feminist_trust += 3; psl_relation -= 6; government_coalition_dissent += 4; far_right_agenda += 3; public_mood_pending_lgbt_equality_support += 10; public_mood_pending_lgbt_equality_left_ownership += 9; news_headline = "The presidential signature opens the next equality campaign"

Kotula thanks the majority that enacted the compromise and announces that the
next bill will concern equal marriage. PSL had expected a period of quiet and
calls the move a breach of political peace. Equality organisations finally see
the partial law described as protection worth using, not gratitude owed to the
parties that stopped short.

- @poland_event_queue: Announce the next bill

@partnership_signed_credit
title: Share credit with PSL and the President
subtitle: Shared ownership protects implementation, but equality organisers will notice how widely Lewica spreads the credit.
view-if: partnership_presidential_outcome = "Signed"
on-arrival: psl_relation += 4; president_relation += 4; public_trust += 2; progressives_dissent += 2; news_headline = "Coalition and Palace jointly defend an enacted compromise"

Kotula, Kosiniak-Kamysz and **[+ president_name +]** appear separately but use
the same language: a limited law, enacted by institutions that disagreed on
more. The shared ownership protects implementation from immediate partisan
reversal. It also blurs who spent years demanding the reform and who agreed
only after reducing it.

- @poland_event_queue: Agree the shared language

