= 14 July 2026 — Procedure without a martyr script

<span class="party-korona"><b>Grzegorz Braun</b></span>, a Korona leader and member of the European Parliament, has
ignored five attempts to complete procedural acts in the separate Oleśnica
hospital investigation. Prosecutor General **[+ justice_minister +]** now asks
the European Parliament to permit Braun's detention long enough to compel an
appearance and hear the charges.

The request concerns six alleged offences, including unlawfully detaining and
making physical contact with a doctor at the hospital. It is not a request for
pre-trial imprisonment, nor is it a verdict in Braun's older seven-count
indictment. [? if braun_legal_preparation >= 8: Earlier documentation, victim
support and count-by-count explanations have left prosecutors a record capable
of surviving political scrutiny.?][? if braun_legal_preparation < 8: Earlier
preparation is thin, leaving Braun room to present several separate files as
one political prosecution.?] Lewica must defend equal process without writing
the martyrdom script for him.

- @braun_warrant
- @braun_surrender
- @braun_case_separation
- @braun_overreach

@braun_warrant
title: Support the immunity request and ordinary compelled appearance
subtitle: Ask Parliament to permit only what five ignored summonses now require, and no more.
on-arrival: {!
Q.braun_compulsion_strategy = "Ordinary compelled appearance";
Q.prosecution_command_clarity += 2;
Q.government_procedural_restraint += 3;
