Q.minority_safety += 2;
Q.news_headline =
    "The compulsion request is defended as ordinary criminal procedure";
!}

Lewica supports the European Parliament request as a narrow step toward an
ordinary interview under criminal procedure. Prosecutors must still prove each
allegation and justify every later restraint. Braun calls the vote political
persecution, but the demand remains stubbornly smaller than the grand trial he
wants to describe.

- @poland_event_queue: Back the request

@braun_surrender
title: Support one final written deadline before compulsion
subtitle: Give Braun a public date, place and consequence so that only his compliance remains in dispute.
on-arrival: braun_compulsion_strategy = "Final written deadline before compulsion"; government_procedural_restraint += 4; braun_martyrdom -= 2; public_trust += 2; prosecution_oversight_capacity += 1; braun_legal_preparation += 1; news_headline = "A final written deadline narrows the dispute to compliance with a summons"

The summons is published with a final date and a precise warning that compelled
appearance follows non-compliance. Victims wait longer, but Braun loses the
claim that an arrest came without an available lawful exit. When the deadline
expires, the European Parliament will be judging a documented refusal rather
than a cloud of prosecutorial rhetoric.

- @poland_event_queue: Publish the final summons

