on-arrival: {!
let severity =
    4 +
    (Number(Q.anti_ukrainian_pressure) || 0) * 0.10 +
    (Number(Q.border_permission_pressure) || 0) * 0.08 +
    Math.max(
        0,
        12 - (Number(Q.refugee_service_capacity) || 0)
    ) * 0.35 +
    Math.max(0, 45 - (Number(Q.minority_safety) || 0)) * 0.10;
if (Q.refugee_settlement == "End alleged Ukrainian preferences") {
    severity += 4;
}
if (Q.asylum_position_2025 == "Supported temporary asylum suspension") {
    severity += 3;
}
if (
    Q.refugee_settlement == "Funded receiving-community services" ||
    Q.refugee_settlement == "Equal and transparent benefit rules"
) {
    severity -= 3;
}
Q.hate_incident_severity_2026 = Math.max(
    3,
    Math.min(20, Math.round(severity))
);
Q.anti_ukrainian_pressure += Q.hate_incident_severity_2026;
Q.minority_safety -= Math.max(
    2,
    Math.round(Q.hate_incident_severity_2026 * 0.55)
);
Q.refugee_empathy -= Math.max(
    1,
    Math.round(Q.hate_incident_severity_2026 * 0.30)
);
Q.public_mood_pending_refugee_solidarity_support += -8;
Q.public_mood_pending_refugee_solidarity_salience += 10;
Q.public_mood_pending_refugee_solidarity_backlash += 9;
Q.news_headline =
    "Anti-Ukrainian hostility crosses from rhetoric into reported incidents";
!}

= October 2026 — More reports do not reveal the whole trend

**Myroslava Keryk**, head of the Ukrainian House foundation, says families are
changing routes to work and deciding which insults are worth reporting. Police
register more anti-Ukrainian incidents, but the increase cannot answer its own
meaning. It may reflect more violence, more trust in reporting, or both; poor
classification can hide either trend.

[? if refugee_service_capacity >= 12 and minority_safety >= 45: Earlier
investment in local services and equal rules has left victims with offices and
people they recognise. The new reports are alarming partly because silence is
no longer the only safe response.?][? if border_permission_pressure >= 45 or
minority_safety < 45: Repeated concessions to collective suspicion have made
anti-Ukrainian rhetoric sound administrative before it becomes violent. Many
victims still expect reporting to create a second danger.?][? if
refugee_service_capacity < 12 and border_permission_pressure < 45 and
minority_safety >= 45: Lewica's earlier record is mixed: it rejected collective
blame without building enough durable local help. Police have a category, but
not yet a trusted route into it.?]

Keryk asks for victim support; police want a usable classification; prosecutors
want files they can prove; border towns want security arguments that do not
license private vengeance. Lewica must decide which institution brings those
demands together.

- @hate_reporting
- @hate_prosecution
- @hate_opposition_bill
- @hate_joint_doctrine
- @hate_denial

@hate_reporting
title: Fund victim reporting, legal aid and transparent classifications
subtitle: Put Ukrainian House and local legal-aid desks between frightened witnesses and an unfamiliar police form. Cost: 1 resource.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: The support network cannot be financed.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; border_response_2026 = "Victim reporting and transparent classification"; minority_safety += 6; police_trust += 3; prosecution_oversight_capacity += 2; anti_ukrainian_pressure -= 2; public_trust += 2; news_headline = "A reporting network makes violence more visible and more prosecutable"

Ukrainian House, municipal lawyers and trained interpreters open one reporting
route, while police publish how incidents are classified and corrected. The
number may rise again as hidden cases enter the record. Victims gain an advocate
and prosecutors gain usable files; Lewica promises not to call visibility a
policy failure merely because it makes the first chart worse.

- @poland_event_queue: Open the reporting route

@hate_prosecution
