= September 2026 — Representation still needs legal authority

<span class="party-lewica"><b>Katarzyna Kotula</b></span>, Lewica's equality advocate, brings the EU gender-balance
duty into a Polish argument about who occupies the rooms where large companies
set pay, investment and employment policy.

[? if boards_law_enacted: Before this meeting, the Sejm majority behind the
functioning cabinet passed the gender-balance transposition and the President
signed it. The statute is already on the books; today's dispute concerns its
implementation and Lewica's next parliamentary demand. The law redistributes
senior corporate power; it does not by itself change pay or give workers a
seat.?]
[? if not boards_law_enacted and caretaker_government: The caretaker can
prepare the transposition file but cannot bind its successor. Lewica has a
proposal and a deadline, not an enacted rule.?]
[? if not boards_law_enacted and not caretaker_government and left_in_government:
The PiS-led cabinet has left the transposition unenacted. Lewica sits inside
that cabinet and must either force a bill onto its agenda or admit the limit of
its ministries.?]
[? if not boards_law_enacted and not caretaker_government and not
left_in_government: [? if government_party = "pis": The PiS-led cabinet has
left the transposition unenacted.?][? if government_party != "pis": The
governing majority has not completed the transposition, and Lewica holds no
cabinet office from which to administer it.?] From opposition, the party can
table and organise around the missing rule; it cannot order company boards to
obey a bill that has not passed.?]

- @boards_defend
- @boards_expand

