!}

[? if horizon_budget_authority: Lewica accepts the Finance Minister's ceiling
after securing money for programmes already enacted. The cabinet's arithmetic
improves and KO gains the discipline it demanded. No new social promise fits;
Razem and unions are asked to defend a year in which survival has replaced
advance.?]
[? if not horizon_budget_authority: The shadow budget shows which expansions
Lewica would postpone while protecting existing entitlements. It saves no state
money until adopted, but it denies the government an easy claim that every
opposition promise assumes an unlimited treasury.?]

- @poland_event_queue: Accept the ceiling

@october_judiciary_horizon
# prose-audit: Grade A — The serving Justice Minister and President enact the conflict without exposing decision scores, Lewica's authority follows its ministry rather than cabinet colour, and all six outcomes receive institutional aftermaths.
title: The judicial-status bill reaches the Palace
subtitle: Appointments, judgments and individual remedies now depend on the President
face-image: img/poland/events/presidential-palace.webp
new-page: true
tags: poland_event
priority: 38
order: 5
max-visits: 1
view-if: continuous_campaign = 1 and year = 2026 and month = 10
on-arrival: {!
Q.judiciary_horizon_cabinet_authority =
    Q.left_in_government && Q.government_has_confidence &&
    !Q.caretaker_government && Q.justice_minister_party == "Lewica" ? 1 : 0;
Q.judicial_repair_mandate += 2;
Q.judiciary_horizon_roll =
    Math.floor((this.random.uint32() / 4294967296) * 11) - 5;
if (Q.judiciary_horizon_cabinet_authority) {
    const horizonHostile = Q.pres_2025_hostile_president || [
        "Andrzej Duda", String(Q.pres_2025_right_candidate || ""),
        "Sławomir Mentzen", "Grzegorz Braun"
    ].includes(Q.president_name);
    Q.judiciary_horizon_score = Math.round(
        44 +
        ((Number(Q.president_relation) || 0) - 35) * 0.35 +
        (Number(Q.president_judiciary_cooperation) || 0) * 0.18 +
        (horizonHostile ? -10 : 8) + Q.judiciary_horizon_roll
    );
    if (Q.judiciary_horizon_score >= 50) {
        Q.judiciary_horizon_presidential_action = "Signed";
        Q.judiciary_status_law_enacted = 1;
        Q.legal_dualism -= 4;
        Q.krs_independence += 3;
        Q.judicial_vacancies -= 2;
Q.public_mood_pending_rule_of_law_salience += 12;
Q.public_mood_pending_rule_of_law_support += 6;
        Q.news_headline =
            Q.president_name + " signs the judicial-status package";
    } else if (Q.judiciary_horizon_score >= 35) {
        Q.judiciary_horizon_presidential_action =
            "Referred to the Constitutional Tribunal";
        Q.judiciary_status_law_enacted = 0;
        Q.court_backlog += 2;
        Q.news_headline =
            Q.president_name + " refers the judicial-status package";
    } else {
        Q.judiciary_horizon_presidential_action = "Vetoed";
        Q.president_veto_count =
            (Number(Q.president_veto_count) || 0) + 1;
        Q.judiciary_status_law_enacted = 0;
        Q.legal_dualism += 2;
        Q.court_backlog += 2;
        Q.news_headline =
            Q.president_name + " vetoes the judicial-status package";
    }
} else {
    Q.judiciary_horizon_score = 0;
    Q.judiciary_horizon_presidential_action = Q.caretaker_government
        ? "No cabinet bill during caretaker government"
        : (Q.government_party == "pis"
            ? "PiS cabinet maintains the disputed system"
            : "Another cabinet controls the bill and Palace response");
    Q.judiciary_status_law_enacted = 0;
    Q.news_headline = Q.judiciary_horizon_presidential_action;
}
!}

= October 2026 — Sign, veto or refer

The proposed status law separates appointment cohorts, preserves most
judgments, restructures disputed chambers and gives individual remedies to
people whose cases carry the institutional conflict.

[? if judiciary_horizon_cabinet_authority: Justice Minister **[+
justice_minister +]**, serving from Lewica, has carried the cabinet bill to **[+
president_name +]**. The President has **[+
judiciary_horizon_presidential_action +]** it. Lewica owns both the ambition of
the text and the duty not to describe a blocked bill as law.?]
[? if not judiciary_horizon_cabinet_authority and caretaker_government: A
caretaker cabinet has not sent a structural bill. Judges and court users remain
on case-by-case remedies until a government wins confidence.?]
[? if not judiciary_horizon_cabinet_authority and not caretaker_government and
left_in_government: Justice Minister **[+ justice_minister +]** is not a Lewica
minister. Status: **[+ judiciary_horizon_presidential_action +]**. Lewica can
press a coalition bill and vote on it, but cannot issue instructions from a
ministry it does not hold.?]
[? if not judiciary_horizon_cabinet_authority and not caretaker_government and
not left_in_government: Justice Minister **[+ justice_minister +]** answers to
another cabinet. Status: **[+ judiciary_horizon_presidential_action +]**.
Lewica may legislate and scrutinise from opposition; it cannot enact, withdraw
or accept a veto for somebody else's government.?]

- @horizon_judicial_bargain
- @horizon_judicial_campaign
- @horizon_judicial_delay
- @horizon_judicial_opposition
- @horizon_judicial_opposition_record
- @horizon_judicial_caretaker

@horizon_judicial_bargain
title: Implement the signed law under a published appointments protocol
subtitle: Publish the sequence, reasons and remedies so implementation cannot become another private personnel bargain.
view-if: judiciary_horizon_cabinet_authority = 1 and judiciary_horizon_presidential_action = "Signed"
on-arrival: president_relation += 3; president_judiciary_cooperation += 4; progressives_dissent += 3; court_user_trust += 3; news_headline = "A signed repair law enters implementation under a published protocol"

The ministry and Palace publish appointment dates, reasons and the route for
individual challenges. Court users can see when the signed law reaches their
case; the President cannot quietly renegotiate its personnel clauses. Lewica's
radicals object that cooperation has preserved too much of the disputed system,
but implementation begins under rules they can inspect.

- @poland_event_queue: Publish the appointment dates

@horizon_judicial_campaign
title: Accept the veto and campaign on the full repair mandate
subtitle: Obey the veto, name the cases it leaves unresolved and seek a new parliamentary mandate.
view-if: judiciary_horizon_cabinet_authority = 1 and judiciary_horizon_presidential_action = "Vetoed"
on-arrival: president_relation -= 8; judicial_repair_mandate += 6; media_capacity += 3; legal_dualism += 3; court_backlog += 3; public_mood_pending_rule_of_law_support += 9; public_mood_pending_rule_of_law_salience += 9; news_headline = "The judicial package becomes a 2027 mandate"

The cabinet does not implement a vetoed statute. Instead, Lewica places judges,
litigants and delayed cases beside the clauses **[+ president_name +]** rejected
and carries the whole package toward 2027. The constitutional line is clean;
the courts still live with vacancies, parallel authorities and another year of
delay.

- @poland_event_queue: Carry the package toward 2027

@horizon_judicial_delay
title: Contest the referral while continuing individual review
subtitle: Challenge the Tribunal route without treating a referred bill as enacted law.
view-if: judiciary_horizon_cabinet_authority = 1 and judiciary_horizon_presidential_action = "Referred to the Constitutional Tribunal"
on-arrival: government_procedural_restraint += 5; european_judgment_compliance += 3; court_backlog += 3; public_trust -= 1; public_mood_pending_rule_of_law_support += -5; public_mood_pending_rule_of_law_left_ownership += -4; news_headline = "The cabinet contests the referral without pretending the bill is law"

The Justice Ministry disputes the competence and composition of the Tribunal
panel, files every argument and keeps individual European-judgment remedies
open. It issues no structural change under the suspended bill. Court users gain
legal honesty and lose time while institutions contest which court may decide
the fate of a law not yet in force.

- @poland_event_queue: Dispute the panel

@horizon_judicial_opposition
title: Publish a Lewica status bill and a court-user remedy ledger
subtitle: Without the Justice Ministry, drafting and casework can expose a route but cannot alter appointments. Cost: 1 resource.
view-if: judiciary_horizon_cabinet_authority = 0 and caretaker_government = 0
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: No legislative and legal team is available.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; judicial_repair_mandate += 3; court_user_trust += 3; constitutional_restraint += 2; media_capacity += 2; public_mood_pending_rule_of_law_support += 8; public_mood_pending_rule_of_law_left_ownership += 7; news_headline = "Lewica publishes the repair it would legislate without claiming cabinet power"

Lewica publishes the full text beside a ledger of vacancies, disputed
appointments and people seeking individual remedies. [? if left_in_government:
The dossier becomes a demand from inside the coalition to Justice Minister **[+
justice_minister +]**; it does not transfer the ministry to us.?][? if not
left_in_government: From opposition, it supplies a bill the cabinet can adopt,
amend or reject and a public record of the cost of doing nothing.?]

- @poland_event_queue: Publish bill and ledger together

@horizon_judicial_opposition_record
title: Table the status bill without a staffed remedy ledger
subtitle: Preserve a parliamentary position without claiming casework, ministerial command or implementation.
view-if: judiciary_horizon_cabinet_authority = 0 and caretaker_government = 0
on-arrival: judicial_repair_mandate += 1; constitutional_restraint += 1; news_headline = "Lewica tables a basic judicial-status bill from opposition"

The club files the clauses and secures a bill number. [? if left_in_government:
Coalition partners must choose whether it receives government time, while the
non-Lewica Justice Minister retains executive authority.?][? if not
left_in_government: The opposition record fixes what Lewica would vote for but
cannot move a single appointment.?] Without a remedy team, affected court users
remain names in the argument rather than clients with help.

- @poland_event_queue: Secure the bill number

@horizon_judicial_caretaker
title: Preserve case-by-case remedies until a cabinet wins confidence
subtitle: Keep files and legal aid alive without asking a caretaker to settle the whole constitutional order.
view-if: judiciary_horizon_cabinet_authority = 0 and caretaker_government = 1
on-arrival: government_procedural_restraint += 2; court_backlog += 2; judicial_vacancies += 1; constitutional_restraint += 2; news_headline = "The caretaker defers a structural bill while courts use individual remedies"

Lewica's lawyers and court-user groups keep individual applications moving while
the caretaker refrains from a structural settlement it cannot carry through
Parliament. Vacancies and backlog grow, but no temporary minister converts an
emergency tenure into a constitutional fait accompli. The next confidence
majority inherits both the unresolved bill and its documented human cost.

- @poland_event_queue: Keep the applications moving

@left_realign_2026
# prose-audit: Grade B — Strong congress framing and a properly authored result, but three of the four merger routes carry no prose at all: federation, Rozwój+ merger and grand merger each set a target string and jump to the tally. Only the keep-allies branch is written.
title: A strong Left convenes the realignment congress
subtitle: Invited centrists, Greens and developmental conservatives decide whether one party is viable
face-image: img/poland/events/left-congress.webp
new-page: true
tags: poland_event
priority: 30
order: 5
max-visits: 1
view-if: continuous_campaign = 1 and year = 2026 and month = 11 and sld_partocracy_stage < 1 and left_poll >= 13 and (left_realign_invite_p2050 = 1 or left_realign_invite_greens = 1 or left_realign_invite_rozwoj = 1)
on-arrival: {!
const federationLegacy = Q.federation_successful ||
    Q.federation_peaceful_unification;
const federationReachBonus = federationLegacy
    ? 8
    : (String(Q.left_merger_structure) == "federation"
        ? Math.max(
            -6,
            3 - (Number(Q.federation_veto_pressure) || 0) * 0.6 -
                (Number(Q.federation_brand_dilution) || 0) * 0.5
        )
        : 0);
Q.left_realign_strength_score = Math.round(
    (Number(Q.left_poll) || 0) * 2 +
    Math.max(0, Number(Q.party_system_left_pull) || 0) * 0.35 +
    (Number(Q.party_unity) || 0) * 0.15 +
    (Number(Q.public_trust) || 0) * 0.10 +
    federationReachBonus
);
Q.left_realign_social_mood = Math.round(
    35 + ((Number(Q.social_spending_support) || 50) - 50) * 0.35 +
    ((Number(Q.economic_issue_salience) || 40) -
        (Number(Q.cultural_issue_salience) || 30)) * 0.25 +
    Math.max(0, Number(Q.party_system_left_pull) || 0) * 0.12
);
const invitedGreens = (Q.rival_group_records || []).find(function(record) {
    return record.id == "greens";
});
Q.left_realign_p2050_score = Math.round(
    (Number(Q.p2050_relation) || 0) +
    Math.max(0, 5 - (Number(Q.p2050_vote_intent) || 0)) * 4 +
    Q.left_realign_strength_score * 0.12 -
    (Number(Q.p2050_coalition_dissent) || 0) * 0.20 +
    federationReachBonus * 0.8
);
Q.left_realign_greens_score = Math.round(
    (Number(invitedGreens && invitedGreens.relation) || 0) +
    Q.left_realign_strength_score * 0.18 +
    Q.left_realign_social_mood * 0.10 +
    federationReachBonus
);
Q.left_realign_rozwoj_score = Math.round(
    (Number(Q.rozwoj_relation) || 0) +
    Q.left_realign_strength_score * 0.16 +
    (Number(Q.left_right_score) || 0) * 0.22 -
    (Number(Q.cultural_issue_salience) || 0) * 0.12 +
    federationReachBonus * 0.5
);
Q.left_realign_p2050_accepted =
    Q.left_realign_invite_p2050 && Number(Q.p2050_seats) > 0 &&
    Q.left_realign_p2050_score >= 55 ? 1 : 0;
Q.left_realign_greens_accepted =
    Q.left_realign_invite_greens && invitedGreens && invitedGreens.active &&
    Q.left_realign_greens_score >= 55 ? 1 : 0;
Q.left_realign_rozwoj_accepted =
    Q.left_realign_invite_rozwoj && Number(Q.rozwoj_seats) > 0 &&
    Q.left_realign_rozwoj_score >= 48 ? 1 : 0;
Q.news_headline = "A strong Lewica tests whether its invitations can become one party";
!}

= November 2026 — From coalition arithmetic to one organisation

We have enough support to convene a congress, but not enough to command it.
Every invitation sent earlier now becomes a decision about dissolving a party,
its name and its parliamentary discipline into a common organisation.

[? if federation_successful = 1: The earlier federation supplies tested rules
for candidate selection, finance, local specialisation and protected identity.
Invited parties therefore see a record of plural organisation rather than only
a promise from Lewica headquarters.?][? if left_merger_structure = "federation"
and federation_successful = 0: The old federal vetoes and competing brands are
also in the room; legal pluralism has not yet proved that it can decide.?][? if
federation_peaceful_unification = 1: The party already showed that a federation
can unify by member consent while preserving its currents.?]

[? if left_realign_invite_p2050 and left_realign_p2050_accepted: Poland 2050's
remaining MPs arrive ready to join. Independence no longer looks like a route
back to the Sejm.?][? if left_realign_invite_p2050 and not
left_realign_p2050_accepted: Poland 2050 accepts electoral cooperation but
refuses liquidation; its MPs still distrust rule from Lewica headquarters.?]
[? if left_realign_invite_greens and left_realign_greens_accepted: The Greens
accept an internal current with their programme and organisers intact.?][? if
left_realign_invite_greens and not left_realign_greens_accepted: The Greens
will share candidates, not their legal identity.?] [? if
left_realign_invite_rozwoj and left_realign_rozwoj_accepted: Rozwój+ believes a
party built around work, welfare and investment can contain its developmental
conservatives.?][? if left_realign_invite_rozwoj and not
left_realign_rozwoj_accepted: Rozwój+ fears that cultural disputes would leave
its MPs as permanent guests on the Left.?]

- @realign_social_federation
- @realign_rozwoj_merger
- @realign_grand_merger
- @realign_keep_allies

@realign_social_federation
title: Unite the invited Poland 2050 and Green currents under Wspólna Polska
view-if: left_realign_invite_p2050 = 1 or left_realign_invite_greens = 1
choose-if: left_realign_strength_score >= 48 and left_realign_social_mood >= 38 and (left_realign_p2050_accepted = 1 or left_realign_greens_accepted = 1)
unavailable-subtitle: The invited organisations still prefer a loose electoral pact.
on-arrival: {!
const targets = [];
if (Q.left_realign_p2050_accepted) targets.push("Poland 2050");
if (Q.left_realign_greens_accepted) targets.push("Zieloni");
Q.left_realign_targets = targets.join(" and ");
!}
go-to: left_realign_result

@realign_rozwoj_merger
title: Merge with Rozwój+ around work, welfare and investment
view-if: left_realign_invite_rozwoj = 1
choose-if: left_realign_strength_score >= 48 and left_right_score >= 42 and cultural_issue_salience <= 50 and rozwoj_relation >= 24 and left_realign_rozwoj_accepted = 1
unavailable-subtitle: The conservative edge or developmental trust is not strong enough.
on-arrival: left_realign_targets = "Rozwój+"
go-to: left_realign_result

@realign_grand_merger
title: Fold Poland 2050, Zieloni and Rozwój+ into one broad party
view-if: left_realign_invite_p2050 = 1 and left_realign_invite_greens = 1 and left_realign_invite_rozwoj = 1
choose-if: left_realign_strength_score >= 60 and left_realign_social_mood >= 42 and left_right_score >= 42 and cultural_issue_salience <= 50 and left_realign_p2050_accepted = 1 and left_realign_greens_accepted = 1 and left_realign_rozwoj_accepted = 1
unavailable-subtitle: A three-way merger needs a dominant Left and a material rather than cultural electoral axis.
on-arrival: left_realign_targets = "Poland 2050, Zieloni and Rozwój+"
go-to: left_realign_result

@realign_keep_allies
title: Keep separate parties under a written electoral coalition
on-arrival: {!
Q.left_realign_targets = "Loose electoral allies";
Q.left_structural_endpoint = String(Q.left_merger_structure) == "federation"
    ? "Expanded federation with loose electoral allies"
    : "Existing party with loose electoral allies";
Q.party_unity += 1;
Q.public_trust += 1;
Q.news_headline = "Lewica keeps its invited partners legally separate";
!}

The delegates choose a common list and a written programme without abolishing
any partner. Our caucus avoids an immediate fight over leadership; every ally
retains the option to leave after the election.

- @poland_event_queue: Sign the electoral coalition

@left_realign_result
title: The realignment becomes one party
new-page: true
on-arrival: {!
const targetText = String(Q.left_realign_targets || "");
const includeP2050 = targetText.includes("Poland 2050") &&
    Boolean(Q.left_realign_p2050_accepted);
const includeGreens = targetText.includes("Zieloni") &&
    Boolean(Q.left_realign_greens_accepted);
const includeRozwoj = targetText.includes("Rozwój+") &&
    Boolean(Q.left_realign_rozwoj_accepted);
const lowEstablishment =
    !Q.barons_active || (Number(Q.barons_strength) || 0) < 25;
const addRealignmentSeatsToLiveCaucus = function(preferred, seats) {
    const amount = Math.max(0, Math.round(Number(seats) || 0));
    if (!amount) return;
    const seatKeys = {
        barons: "left_barons_seats",
        spring: "left_spring_seats",
        labor: "left_labor_seats",
        progressives: "left_progressives_seats",
        razem: "razem_seats",
        pps: "left_pps_seats",
        social_patriot: "left_social_patriot_seats"
    };
    const candidates = [
        preferred, "progressives", "labor", "social_patriot", "barons",
        "spring", "razem", "pps"
    ];
    let target = candidates.find(function(id, index) {
        return candidates.indexOf(id) == index &&
            Q[id + "_active"] && Q[id + "_in_left"];
    });
    if (!target) {
        target = preferred;
        Q[target + "_active"] = 1;
        Q[target + "_in_left"] = 1;
        Q[target + "_party_formed"] = 0;
        Q[target + "_strength"] = Math.max(
            5,
            Number(Q[target + "_strength"]) || 0
        );
    }
    Q[seatKeys[target]] =
        Math.max(0, Number(Q[seatKeys[target]]) || 0) + amount;
};
if (includeRozwoj) {
    Q.left_realign_name = lowEstablishment
        ? "Nowa Solidarność"
        : (includeP2050 || includeGreens
            ? "Solidarność Społeczna"
            : "Lewica Rozwoju");
} else {
    Q.left_realign_name = "Wspólna Polska";
}
Q.left_realign_formed = 1;
const federationOrigin =
    String(Q.left_merger_structure) == "federation" ||
    Boolean(Q.federation_successful) ||
    Boolean(Q.federation_peaceful_unification);
let transferredSeats = 0;
let transferredP2050CabinetOffice = 0;
if (includeP2050 && !Q.p2050_joined_left) {
    const p2050Transfer = Math.max(0, Number(Q.p2050_seats) || 0);
    const p2050WasSupportingGovernment =
        Q.government_has_confidence && !Q.caretaker_government &&
        (
            Q.government_party == "p2050" ||
            Boolean(Q.ministry_p2050_in_cabinet)
        );
    if (Q.unia_centrum_formed && (Number(Q.centrum_seats) || 0) > 0) {
        Q.centrum_independent_vote_base = Math.max(
            Number(Q.centrum_independent_vote_base) || 0,
            Number(Q.centrum_vote_intent) || 0,
            Number(Q.centrum_poll) || 0,
            Number(Q.centrum_seats) * 100 / 460 * 0.72
        );
    }
    const cabinetPortfolios = [
        "labor", "equality", "housing", "health", "digital", "science",
        "interior", "finance", "economy", "justice", "foreign",
        "agriculture", "defence"
    ];
    for (const portfolio of cabinetPortfolios) {
        if (Q[portfolio + "_minister_party"] == "Poland 2050") {
            Q[portfolio + "_minister_party"] = "Lewica";
            transferredP2050CabinetOffice = 1;
        }
    }
    Q.p2050_joined_left = 1;
    Q.left_p2050_current_seats = p2050Transfer;
    Q.p2050_seats = 0;
    Q.p2050_loyalist_seats = 0;
    Q.p2050_liberal_seats = 0;
    Q.p2050_independent_seats = 0;
    Q.p2050_ai_active = 0;
    Q.ministry_p2050_in_cabinet = 0;
    Q.third_way_active = 0;
    Q.third_way_split = 1;
    if (p2050WasSupportingGovernment) {
        Q.government_support_seats = Math.max(
            0,
            (Number(Q.government_support_seats) || 0) - p2050Transfer
        );
    }
    addRealignmentSeatsToLiveCaucus("progressives", p2050Transfer);
    transferredSeats += p2050Transfer;
}
if (includeGreens && !Q.greens_joined_left && !Q.p2050_greens_absorbed) {
    const greens = (Q.rival_group_records || []).find(function(record) {
        return record.id == "greens";
    });
    const greenTransfer = Math.min(
        Math.max(0, Number(Q.ko_seats) || 0),
        Math.max(0, Number(greens && greens.exclusive_seats) ||
            Number(greens && greens.mp_count) || 0)
    );
    Q.greens_joined_left = 1;
    Q.left_green_current_seats = greenTransfer;
    Q.ko_seats -= greenTransfer;
    if (
        Q.government_party == "ko" &&
        Q.government_has_confidence && !Q.caretaker_government
    ) {
        Q.government_support_seats = Math.max(
            0,
            (Number(Q.government_support_seats) || 0) - greenTransfer
        );
    }
    addRealignmentSeatsToLiveCaucus("progressives", greenTransfer);
    transferredSeats += greenTransfer;
    if (greens) {
        greens.bloc = "left";
        greens.kind = "current";
        greens.parent = Q.left_realign_name;
        greens.legal_status = "internal green current";
        greens.exclusive_seats = 0;
    }
}
if (includeRozwoj && !Q.rozwoj_joined_left) {
    const rozwojTransfer = Math.max(0, Number(Q.rozwoj_seats) || 0);
    const rozwoj = (Q.rival_group_records || []).find(function(record) {
        return record.id == "rozwoj_plus";
    });
    Q.rozwoj_joined_left = 1;
    Q.left_rozwoj_current_seats = rozwojTransfer;
    Q.rozwoj_seats = 0;
    if (
        Q.government_party == "pis" &&
        Q.government_has_confidence && !Q.caretaker_government
    ) {
        Q.government_support_seats = Math.max(
            0,
            (Number(Q.government_support_seats) || 0) - rozwojTransfer
        );
    }
    addRealignmentSeatsToLiveCaucus("labor", rozwojTransfer);
    transferredSeats += rozwojTransfer;
    if (Q.matysiak_party == "rozwoj") {
        Q.matysiak_party = "left";
        Q.matysiak_status = Q.left_realign_name + " developmental-current MP";
    }
    if (rozwoj) {
        rozwoj.bloc = "left";
        rozwoj.kind = "current";
        rozwoj.parent = Q.left_realign_name;
        rozwoj.legal_status = "internal developmental current";
        rozwoj.exclusive_seats = 0;
    }
}
Q.left_seats = Math.max(0, Number(Q.left_seats) || 0) + transferredSeats;
Q.left_new_generation_seats =
    Math.max(0, Number(Q.left_labor_seats) || 0) +
    Math.max(0, Number(Q.left_progressives_seats) || 0);
Q.nowa_lewica_seats =
    Math.max(0, Number(Q.left_barons_seats) || 0) +
    Math.max(0, Number(Q.left_spring_seats) || 0) +
    Math.max(0, Number(Q.left_labor_seats) || 0) +
    Math.max(0, Number(Q.left_progressives_seats) || 0);
Q.left_party_name = Q.left_realign_name;
Q.nowa_lewica_merger_agreed = 1;
Q.left_common_party_exists = 1;
Q.left_merger_structure = "unified_party";
Q.left_merger_scope = "realignment_congress";
Q.left_constitution = "protected_currents";
Q.left_machine_controller = "shared";
Q.left_mandate = "realignment_congress";
Q.left_pluralism_protected = 1;
Q.left_structural_endpoint =
    Q.left_realign_name + " — plural unified party";
if (federationOrigin) {
    Q.federation_successful = 1;
    Q.federation_peaceful_unification = 1;
    Q.federation_crisis_result =
        "Federal experience completed a peaceful plural realignment";
}
for (const current of ["barons", "spring", "razem", "pps"]) {
    if (Q[current + "_active"] && Q[current + "_in_left"]) {
        Q[current + "_org_status"] = "merged_current";
    }
}
Q.barons_merged = Q.barons_active && Q.barons_in_left ? 1 : Q.barons_merged;
Q.spring_merged = Q.spring_active && Q.spring_in_left ? 1 : Q.spring_merged;
Q.razem_merged = Q.razem_active && Q.razem_in_left ? 1 : Q.razem_merged;
if (transferredP2050CabinetOffice) {
    Q.left_in_government = 1;
    Q.left_cabinet_committed = 1;
    Q.left_cabinet_model =
        "Broad realignment party in the governing coalition";
    Q.ministry_left_cabinet_seats = Q.left_seats;
    Q.ministries_finalized = 1;
    Q.position = "Governing coalition";
    Q.budget = Math.max(1, Number(Q.budget) || 0);
    Q.budget_authority =
        "Governing coalition — inherited realignment portfolios";
    if (Q.government_party == "p2050") {
        Q.government_party = "lewica";
        Q.government_owner = Q.left_realign_name + "-led cabinet";
        Q.cabinet_roster_government_party = "lewica";
    }
}
Q.party_unity += includeRozwoj ? -3 : 3;
Q.progressives_dissent += includeRozwoj ? 6 : -2;
Q.barons_dissent += lowEstablishment ? 7 : 2;
Q.news_headline = Q.left_realign_name + " forms with " + targetText;
!}

= [+ left_realign_name +]

The joined MPs now sit in one seat ledger. Their former parties survive only
as named internal currents; separate polling and coalition arithmetic are
over. [? if p2050_joined_left: Poland 2050's survivors become a centrist
current inside our parliamentary club.?] [? if greens_joined_left: The Greens
gain an organised current but surrender their separate bargain with KO.?] [? if
rozwoj_joined_left: Rozwój+ brings its MPs and its argument for a more
developmental, culturally cautious Left.?] The first congress inherits those
differences; unity on paper has not made them disappear.

[? if federation_peaceful_unification: The old federation ends by consent, not
administrative absorption. Its candidate, finance and arbitration rules become
the protected-current statute of **[+ left_realign_name +]**.?]

- @left_realign_finish

@left_realign_finish
title: Open the new party's first congress
go-to: poland_event_queue

@independence_2026
# prose-audit: Grade A — Kaczyński, Mentzen, Braun, Morawiecki and the March Association compete through named organisations, Lewica's accumulated street strategy is narrated rather than counted, and all four choices have role-correct aftermaths.
title: The 2026 Independence Day March
subtitle: PiS, Konfederacja, Braun and a possible Morawiecki bloc compete
face-image: img/poland/events/independence-march-2021.webp
new-page: true
tags: poland_event
priority: 26
order: 10
max-visits: 1
view-if: continuous_campaign = 1 and year = 2026 and month = 11
on-arrival: last_independence_march_year = 2026; far_right_street_capacity += 4; public_mood_pending_refugee_solidarity_support += -5; public_mood_pending_refugee_solidarity_backlash += 6; news_headline = "A fragmented right turns Independence Day into a leadership primary"

= November 2026 — The right competes for the march

The Independence March Association still controls the route and much of the
stage, but it no longer controls the political meaning alone. **Jarosław
Kaczyński's PiS** wants the national-conservative inheritance; **Sławomir
Mentzen's Konfederacja** wants the young crowd; [? if president_name =
"Grzegorz Braun": President **Grzegorz Braun's** Korona supporters want the day
to ratify the movement that carried him to the Palace.?][? if president_name !=
"Grzegorz Braun": **Grzegorz Braun's Korona** wants a more radical column and
another confrontation around its leader.?] [? if rozwoj_club_formed or
rozwoj_party_formed: **Mateusz Morawiecki's Rozwój+** claims a developmental,
respectable patriotism distinct from Kaczyński without surrendering the right's
symbols.?]

Those columns can radicalise one another or expose how many leaders now claim
one march. Lewica arrives with memory rather than a clean slate. [? if
independence_march_strategy = "Civic tradition": Our civic ceremonies have
begun to acquire organisers, families and rituals of their own.?][? if
independence_march_strategy = "Legal monitoring": Observers and victim-support
lawyers return with an annual record the police know they will have to answer.?]
[? if independence_march_strategy = "Join the Independence March": Our previous
entry proved that a social-patriotic Left column can appear inside the march and
that doing so can split Lewica before it splits the right.?][? if
independence_march_strategy = "Counter-mobilisation" or
independence_march_strategy = "Exploit right fragmentation": Earlier
counter-mobilisation filled streets and cameras while helping every rival column
claim an emergency.?][? if independence_march_strategy = "Ignore the march" or
independence_march_strategy = "No strategy": We have left no durable November
institution behind; anything built this year begins late.?]

- @ind26_reclaimed
- @ind26_civic
- @ind26_join_pluralized
- @ind26_join
- @ind26_monitor_institution
- @ind26_rules
- @ind26_counter_coalition
- @ind26_divide

@ind26_reclaimed
title: Lead Poland's largest Independence Day march
subtitle: The permanent civic network pays its own costs. Turn five earlier commemorations into the day's main national procession.
view-if: civic_independence_investment >= 3 and civic_independence_years >= 5 and independence_day_reclaimed = 0
on-arrival: independence_march_strategy = "Civic tradition"; independence_day_reclaimed = 1; civic_independence_years += 1; civic_patriotism += 12; local_network += 5; public_trust += 5; minority_safety += 3; far_right_street_capacity -= 8; far_right_agenda -= 4; news_headline = "Poland's largest Independence Day march is now the democratic civic procession"

= Independence Day has been reclaimed

The municipal committees, unions, veterans, choirs and family groups no longer
assemble as a smaller answer to somebody else's event. Their own dues,
collections and local institutions cover the route, stages, stewards and
transport without another grant from party headquarters.

When the counts arrive, ours is the largest Independence Day procession in
Poland. Families fill the route behind the white-and-red flag, Daszyński's
republican inheritance and a promise that citizenship is not an ethnic test.
The Independence March Association still marches, but it has become the rival
event: one nationalist column among several claimants, no longer the national
default.

The holiday has not been reclaimed by a ban or a police order. It has been
reclaimed because the alternative outgrew the monopoly.

- @poland_event_queue: Carry the reclaimed holiday forward

@ind26_civic
title: Stage the strongest civic-independence alternative yet
subtitle: Give unions, veterans, municipalities and families a commemoration whose existence does not depend on the nationalist route. [? if civic_independence_investment >= 3: The permanent network pays its own costs.?][? if civic_independence_investment < 3: Cost: 2 resources.?]
view-if: civic_independence_investment < 3 or civic_independence_years < 5 or independence_day_reclaimed = 1
choose-if: civic_independence_investment >= 3 or resources >= 2
unavailable-subtitle: The organisation cannot mount a national commemoration.
on-arrival: resources -= 2 if civic_independence_investment < 3; civic_independence_investment += 2 if civic_independence_investment < 3; independence_march_strategy = "Civic tradition"; civic_independence_years += 1; civic_patriotism += 8; local_network += 4; public_trust += 3; far_right_street_capacity -= 2; news_headline = "A democratic independence tradition becomes an institution"

Municipal leaders, veterans of democratic movements, unions and school choirs
take a separate route with their own wreaths and speakers. It is not merely a
counter-protest timed by Braun or Mentzen. Families can attend without entering
a nationalist leadership contest, and local organisers leave with a calendar
for next year rather than a photograph from one Warsaw afternoon.

- @poland_event_queue: Set the route

@ind26_join_pluralized
title: Make our permanent column a co-organiser of the main march
subtitle: Four earlier entries have built stewards, speakers and a constituency the Association can no longer remove without splitting its own procession.
view-if: independence_join_years >= 4 and independence_main_march_pluralized = 0
on-arrival: independence_march_strategy = "Join the Independence March"; independence_main_march_pluralized = 1; independence_join_years += 1; civic_patriotism += 8; social_patriot_support += 13; labor_credibility += 4; rural_support += 4; public_trust += 2; minority_safety += 1; progressives_dissent += 5; party_unity -= 1; far_right_street_capacity -= 3; far_right_fragmentation += 9; news_headline = "The permanent Left column forces the main march into plural ownership"

= The march no longer has one owner

Years of returning under the same labour, republican and public-service banners
have produced our own stewards, transport, speakers and crowd. When the
Association tries to exclude them, municipal partners and part of the march's
union contingent threaten a separate route. The organisers retreat rather than
preside over a visibly smaller procession.

Lewica's column receives its own assembly liaison, stage time and authority over
its section of the route. It has not made the nationalist organisations
democratic, and progressives still dispute the bargain. It has made their old
claim to sole ownership impossible: the main march is now a negotiated coalition
whose largest organised bloc speaks about wages, service and a social republic.

- @poland_event_queue: Record the plural march

@ind26_join
title: Enter the main march and bid for its social-patriotic leadership
subtitle: The caucus can split the right's columns, but risks splitting Lewica first.
view-if: independence_join_years < 4 or independence_main_march_pluralized = 1
on-arrival: independence_march_strategy = "Join the Independence March"; independence_join_years += 1; civic_patriotism += 6; social_patriot_support += 11; left_cultural_position += 5; left_right_score += 5; rural_support += 3; progressives_dissent += 10; spring_dissent += 8; razem_dissent += 7; minority_safety -= 3; far_right_street_capacity += 2; far_right_fragmentation += 5; party_unity -= 2; news_headline = "The social-patriotic Left enters a fragmented march and opens a rupture at home"

Lewica's social patriots enter under labour, republican and military-service
banners and refuse to march behind any party leader. They force Kaczyński,
Mentzen, Braun and Morawiecki to compete for ownership in full view. The crowd
grows around the contest; minority groups see our flags inside a space they
still experience as threatening, and progressives begin an internal revolt
before the last column leaves the roundabout.

- @poland_event_queue: Enter under our own banners

@ind26_monitor_institution
title: Turn the annual monitoring operation into a permanent safety institution
subtitle: Four earlier deployments have built the lawyers, evidence rules and public trust needed to operate without improvisation.
view-if: independence_monitor_years >= 4 and independence_monitor_institution = 0
on-arrival: independence_march_strategy = "Legal monitoring"; independence_monitor_institution = 1; independence_monitor_years += 1; police_trust += 6; minority_safety += 8; constitutional_restraint += 6; public_trust += 3; media_capacity += 3; far_right_street_capacity -= 4; braun_martyrdom -= 2; news_headline = "A permanent Independence Day safety institution replaces the annual emergency operation"

= The route has an institution watching it

The hotline, accredited observers, medics, evidence archive and victim lawyers
now open on a standing calendar rather than after each new threat. Residents,
journalists and police commanders all know the same liaison points and retention
rules before the first column assembles.

[? if left_in_government and interior_minister_party = "Lewica": The Interior
Ministry incorporates those tested rules into a neutral annual protocol without
placing the civic organisation under party command.?][? if not left_in_government
or interior_minister_party != "Lewica": The independent network remains outside
the chain of command, but its accumulated record is strong enough that the
serving ministry must answer departures in real time.?] Protection is no longer
the fragile side effect of one year's political attention.

- @poland_event_queue: Open the permanent safety ledger

@ind26_rules
title: [? if left_in_government and interior_minister_party = "Lewica": Issue neutral assembly rules and fund victim protection?][? if not left_in_government or interior_minister_party != "Lewica": Publish an independent monitoring and victim-protection plan?]
subtitle: Use only the authority Lewica actually holds; a civic monitor cannot command police and a minister cannot choose the lawful message.
view-if: independence_monitor_years < 4 or independence_monitor_institution = 1
on-arrival: independence_march_strategy = "Legal monitoring"; independence_monitor_years += 1; police_trust += 4; minority_safety += 5; constitutional_restraint += 3; public_trust += 1; news_headline = "The state refuses to choose among right-wing ownership claims"

[? if left_in_government and interior_minister_party = "Lewica": Interior
Minister **[+ interior_minister +]** publishes one assembly standard, liaison
points and victim-protection teams for every column. Police protect routes and
people without awarding the state seal to any claimant.?][? if not
left_in_government or interior_minister_party != "Lewica": Lewica funds legal
observers, hotlines and victim support, then submits the same neutral rules to
the serving Interior Minister. We can document compliance and demand command
decisions; we cannot issue police orders.?] Each right-wing leader must now
compete politically rather than for privileged enforcement.

- @poland_event_queue: Publish the standard

@ind26_counter_coalition
title: Activate the standing democratic street coalition
subtitle: Three earlier counter-mobilisations have built a coalition that can protect its own route without draining every organisation for one emergency.
view-if: independence_counter_years >= 3 and independence_counter_coalition = 0
on-arrival: independence_march_strategy = "Counter-mobilisation"; independence_counter_coalition = 1; independence_counter_years += 1; organiser_energy += 2; progressive_credibility += 7; minority_safety += 7; civic_patriotism += 3; public_trust += 3; far_right_street_capacity -= 4; far_right_agenda -= 2; braun_martyrdom -= 2; news_headline = "A standing democratic coalition out-organises the radical-right columns"

= Mobilisation becomes capacity

Anti-fascist groups, unions, neighbourhood organisations and minority networks
no longer rebuild their command structure each November. Shared stewards,
transport, medics and local assemblies put a larger democratic force beside the
people the nationalist columns once expected to isolate.

Because the coalition has its own route and public programme, Braun and Mentzen
cannot turn a hurried blockade into their organising story. The counter-march
protects threatened communities, keeps its organisers for the work after the
holiday and leaves the radical right facing a stronger street rather than a
larger emergency audience.

- @poland_event_queue: Carry the coalition beyond November

@ind26_divide
title: Amplify every split on the right
subtitle: Turn rival stages, insults and route disputes into a week-long leadership spectacle.
view-if: independence_counter_years < 3 or independence_counter_coalition = 1
on-arrival: independence_march_strategy = "Exploit right fragmentation"; independence_counter_years += 1; media_capacity += 3; far_right_fragmentation += 5; far_right_street_capacity += 3; braun_martyrdom += 2; public_trust -= 1; news_headline = "The Left wins a tactical media week and helps fill every radical-right column"

Lewica's media team clips every quarrel over speakers, symbols and precedence.
Kaczyński, Mentzen, Braun and Morawiecki each receive the humiliation of being
shown as one claimant among several—and the free publicity needed to summon a
larger column. We win the week's commentary while Warsaw inherits more
mobilised organisations than it had before our cameras arrived.

- @poland_event_queue: Start clipping

@constructive_motion_2026
# prose-audit: Grade A — The constructive motion centres the named replacement, real defections and Lewica's coalition role rather than forecast-score manipulation.
title: A constructive no-confidence motion
subtitle: The opposition tests a constructive no-confidence motion
face-image: img/poland/events/sejm-chamber.webp
new-page: true
tags: poland_event
priority: 30
order: 5
max-visits: 1
view-if: continuous_campaign = 1 and year = 2026 and month = 11 and government_party != "pis" and government_has_confidence = 1 and caretaker_government = 0 and formation_in_progress = 0 and (government_coalition_dissent >= 45 or early_election_risk >= 45 or coalition_broken = 1)
on-arrival: {!
const pisSeats = Math.max(0, Number(Q.pis_seats) || 0);
const morawieckiCamp = Math.max(
    0,
    Number(Q.pis_morawiecki_camp) || 0
);
const sikorskiDemocraticSeats =
    Math.max(0, Number(Q.ko_seats) || 0) +
    Math.max(0, Number(Q.psl_seats) || 0) +
    Math.max(0, Number(Q.p2050_seats) || 0) +
    Math.max(0, Number(Q.centrum_seats) || 0);
const sikorskiBlocSeats = sikorskiDemocraticSeats +
    Math.max(0, Number(Q.konf_seats) || 0);
const hostileDemocraticPartners = [
    [Q.ko_seats, Q.ko_relation],
    [Q.psl_seats, Q.psl_relation],
    [Q.p2050_seats, Q.p2050_relation],
    [Q.centrum_seats, Q.centrum_relation]
].filter(function(party) {
    return Number(party[0]) > 0 && Number(party[1]) <= 30;
}).length;
const sikorskiRoute =
    Q.government_party == "lewica" &&
    Q.left_in_government &&
    Q.ministry_ko_in_cabinet &&
    Q.president_name != "Radosław Sikorski" &&
    Q.prime_minister != "Radosław Sikorski" &&
    (Number(Q.government_coalition_dissent) || 0) >= 60 &&
    hostileDemocraticPartners >= 2 &&
    (Number(Q.konf_seats) || 0) > 0 &&
    sikorskiBlocSeats >= 231;
if (sikorskiRoute) {
    Q.constructive_candidate = "Radosław Sikorski";
    Q.constructive_base = sikorskiBlocSeats;
    Q.constructive_nomination_reason =
        "KO and the estranged democratic partners accept Konfederacja's votes to remove the Left-led cabinet.";
} else if (Q.pis_split || morawieckiCamp >= 25) {
    Q.constructive_candidate = "Mateusz Morawiecki";
    Q.constructive_base =
        pisSeats +
        (Q.pis_split ? morawieckiCamp : 0) +
        Math.round((Number(Q.p2050_seats) || 0) * 0.15) +
        Math.round((Number(Q.psl_seats) || 0) * 0.10);
    Q.constructive_nomination_reason =
        "The Morawiecki camp claims it can recruit the centre.";
} else if ((Number(Q.far_right_agenda) || 0) >= 45) {
    Q.constructive_candidate = "Przemysław Czarnek";
    Q.constructive_base =
        pisSeats +
        Math.round((Number(Q.konf_seats) || 0) * 0.65);
    Q.constructive_nomination_reason =
        "PiS hardliners choose a culture-war route to 231.";
} else {
    Q.constructive_candidate = "Beata Szydło";
    Q.constructive_base =
        pisSeats +
        Math.round((Number(Q.psl_seats) || 0) * 0.25);
    Q.constructive_nomination_reason =
        "The opposition tries to recruit rural deputies with a welfare-nationalist offer.";
}
Q.news_headline =
    "The opposition files a constructive motion naming " +
    Q.constructive_candidate;
!}

= November 2026 — Dismissal requires a replacement

At least 46 sponsors must name a candidate, and 231 deputies must vote for that
person. A failed motion does not dissolve the Sejm.

[? if constructive_candidate = "Radosław Sikorski": KO, the estranged
democratic coalition parties and Konfederacja have named <span class="party-ko"><b>Radosław Sikorski</b></span>.
The agreement gives the radical right cabinet offices in exchange for replacing
Lewica immediately.?][? if constructive_candidate != "Radosław Sikorski": The
opposition—not Lewica—has named **[+ constructive_candidate +]**.?]
[+ constructive_nomination_reason +] Its published starting count is **[+
constructive_base +]**. [? if constructive_candidate != "Radosław Sikorski":
Low PSL/Poland 2050 relations and coalition dissent can still add defections at
the roll call.?]

- @constructive_sikorski
- @constructive_morawiecki
- @constructive_czarnek
- @constructive_szydlo
- @constructive_defend_2026

@constructive_sikorski
title: Publish the secret Konfederacja annex
subtitle: Force every democratic-party deputy to defend the ministries traded for the radical right's votes.
view-if: constructive_candidate = "Radosław Sikorski"
on-arrival: constructive_base -= 6; media_capacity += 4; public_trust += 2; far_right_agenda -= 2; news_headline = "Lewica publishes the Konfederacja annex behind Sikorski's motion"

The signatures reveal the price: Finance and Economy for Konfederacja, a
moratorium on Lewica's social programme and a first-session repeal calendar.
Six deputies retreat. The remaining signatories decide that removing the Left
is worth making the bargain public.

- @constructive_roll_2026: Bring the named replacement to a roll call

@constructive_morawiecki
title: Publish the nominee's recruitment ledger
subtitle: Make every promised office public and force recruits to defend the bargain.
on-arrival: constructive_base -= 8; media_capacity += 3; public_trust += 1; news_headline = "The Left names every promised office behind the replacement motion"

We name the committee chairs, ministries and local promises behind the motion.
Several recruits retreat rather than defend the bargain; the nominee can no
longer present every prospective vote as ideological conversion.

