@snap_budget_deadline
title: Petition the President after the four-month budget deadline
subtitle: The Palace decides independently whether to shorten the term.
choose-if: snap_budget_deadline_ready = 1
unavailable-subtitle: Four months have not elapsed since the recorded draft-budget submission.
on-arrival: snap_election_trigger = "Article 225 petition after the budget deadline"; snap_budget_petition_advocacy = 4; president_relation -= 1; public_trust -= 1; news_headline = "The Article 225 petition reaches the President"
go-to: snap_budget_palace_decision

@snap_budget_palace_decision
title: The Palace decides under Article 225
new-page: true
on-arrival: {!
Q.snap_budget_petition_roll =
    Math.floor((this.random.uint32() / 4294967296) * 11) - 5;
const hostileToCabinet =
    (
        Q.pres_2025_hostile_president &&
        Q.government_party != "pis"
    ) ||
    (
        Q.president_name == "Andrzej Duda" &&
        Q.government_party != "pis"
    ) ||
    (
        Q.president_name == "Rafał Trzaskowski" &&
        Q.government_party == "pis"
    );
Q.snap_budget_petition_score = Math.round(
    (Number(Q.early_election_risk) || 0) * 0.30 +
    (Number(Q.government_coalition_dissent) || 0) * 0.25 +
    Math.max(0, 50 - (Number(Q.public_trust) || 0)) * 0.20 +
    (hostileToCabinet ? 14 : -4) +
    (Number(Q.snap_budget_petition_advocacy) || 0) +
    Q.snap_budget_petition_roll
);
Q.snap_budget_petition_approved =
    Q.snap_budget_petition_score >= 35 ? 1 : 0;
Q.news_headline = Q.snap_budget_petition_approved
    ? "The President decides to shorten the Sejm term"
    : "The President declines to shorten the Sejm term";
!}

Our petition forces a decision, not an election. The President weighs the
cabinet's disorder, the public cost of another campaign and the advantage the
Palace expects from acting now.

[? if snap_budget_petition_approved: The President signs the order shortening
the term. Parties leave the Palace for an election they can no longer defer.?]
[? if not snap_budget_petition_approved: The President refuses. The failed
budget remains the cabinet's burden, and our demand has exposed how little
control we have over the Palace.?]

- @snap_budget_approved
- @snap_budget_declined

@snap_budget_approved
title: Record the presidential shortening
view-if: snap_budget_petition_approved = 1
on-arrival: snap_election_trigger = "Presidential shortening after the budget deadline"; budget_deadline_active = 0; court_user_trust += 1; public_trust -= 1; news_headline = "The President uses Article 225 to shorten the term"
go-to: snap_campaign_launch

@snap_budget_declined
title: Record the President's refusal
view-if: snap_budget_petition_approved = 0
on-arrival: {!
Q.snap_election_requested = 0;
Q.budget_deadline_active = 0;
Q.early_election_risk = Math.max(
    35,
    Q.early_election_risk - 15
);
Q.president_relation -= 2;
Q.news_headline =
    "The Article 225 window closes without an election";
!}
go-to: poland_event_queue

@snap_formation_ladder
title: Enter the three constitutional formation attempts
subtitle: Available to a Lewica cabinet that resigns, or when a caretaker already requires formation.
view-if: snap_left_can_resign_cabinet = 1
on-arrival: snap_formation_attempt = 1; snap_formation_context = "Pre-election dissolution ladder"; snap_left_cabinet_commitment = 0; snap_cabinet_commitments_recorded = 0; snap_psl_cabinet_committed = 0; snap_p2050_cabinet_committed = 0; snap_centrum_cabinet_committed = 0; caretaker_government = 1; government_has_confidence = 0; constitutional_restraint += 1; public_trust -= 1; news_headline = "The caretaker period opens the first constitutional formation attempt"
go-to: snap_formation_attempt_one

@snap_campaign_launch
title: The dissolution opens a campaign
subtitle: The vote is next month, not on the day the term ends
new-page: true
on-arrival: {!
Q.snap_campaign_active = 1;
// A dissolution before the ordinary term ends means the 2021-2023 dated
// calendar no longer describes this timeline, and the events that assume it
// stop firing.
if (Number(Q.year) < 2023 ||
    (Number(Q.year) == 2023 && Number(Q.month) <= 7)) {
    Q.historical_2023_calendar = 0;
}
Q.snap_campaign_start_time = Number(Q.time) || 0;
Q.snap_campaign_due_time = Q.snap_campaign_start_time + 1;
Q.snap_campaign_start_year = Number(Q.year) || 0;
Q.snap_campaign_start_month = Number(Q.month) || 0;
Q.snap_campaign_beyond_horizon =
    Q.snap_campaign_start_year > 2027 ||
    Q.snap_campaign_start_year == 2027 &&
        Q.snap_campaign_start_month >= 10 ? 1 : 0;
Q.snap_campaign_strategy = "Unchosen";
Q.snap_campaign_left_bonus = 0;
Q.snap_election_requested = 0;
Q.snap_election_held = 0;
Q.snap_election_complete = 0;
Q.budget_deadline_active = 0;
Q.caretaker_government = 1;
Q.government_has_confidence = 0;
Q.formation_complete = 0;
Q.formation_in_progress = 0;
Q.early_election_risk = 100;
Q.position = "Snap-election campaign";
Q.news_headline = "Dissolution starts a month-long election campaign";
!}

The legal trigger was **[+ snap_election_trigger +]**. The outgoing cabinet
now serves in a caretaker role. Ballots are counted only after a campaign month
has passed. [? if snap_campaign_beyond_horizon: Because dissolution occurred
at or after October 2027, the constitutional timetable pushes polling day into
the next year. The outgoing cabinet remains in care until voters choose a new
Sejm.?]

- @snap_campaign_social
- @snap_campaign_democratic
- @snap_campaign_independent

@snap_campaign_social
title: Campaign on wages, housing and public services
subtitle: Give our organizers a distinct offer and make material security the election's dividing line.
on-arrival: snap_campaign_strategy = "Material security"; snap_campaign_left_bonus = 1.3; labor_credibility += 3; economic_issue_salience += 4; public_mood_pending_social_spending_support += 10; public_mood_pending_social_spending_salience += 9; news_headline = "Lewica makes material security the snap-election argument"

Union halls and tenant groups finally hear a campaign built around their own
demands. KO warns that we are turning a constitutional election into a contest
inside the opposition.

- @poland_regional_campaign.snap_open: Put it on the regional map

@snap_campaign_democratic
title: Defend a joint democratic majority
subtitle: Reassure coalition voters, even if Lewica's own programme becomes less distinct.
on-arrival: snap_campaign_strategy = "Democratic majority"; snap_campaign_left_bonus = 0.6; ko_relation += 5; coalition_clarity += 2; party_unity -= 1; news_headline = "Lewica campaigns as the social pillar of a democratic majority"

KO welcomes us back onto a common stage. Our candidates gain a clear coalition
answer at every debate, while activists grumble that voters are again being
asked to save someone else's government.

- @poland_regional_campaign.snap_open: Put it on the regional map

@snap_campaign_independent
title: Run against both conservative blocs
subtitle: Rally the party behind its own banner and accept a colder relationship with KO.
on-arrival: snap_campaign_strategy = "Independent Left"; snap_campaign_left_bonus = 1; party_unity += 2; ko_relation -= 4; progressive_credibility += 2; news_headline = "Lewica fights the snap election under its own banner"

Our factions close ranks around an autonomous Left campaign. KO responds by
treating every vote we take from it as a threat to the next majority.

- @poland_regional_campaign.snap_open: Put it on the regional map

@snap_campaign_result_due_2026
# prose-audit: Grade B — A clean three-line handoff into the count, well voiced from the campaign's side; it is a transition beat rather than an event, with no decision of its own.
title: The snap-election campaign reaches polling day
subtitle: One month has passed since dissolution
face-image: img/poland/events/election-2023-ballot.webp
new-page: true
tags: poland_event
priority: 60
order: 1
max-visits: 2
view-if: continuous_campaign = 1 and snap_campaign_active = 1 and time >= snap_campaign_due_time

One month after **[+ snap_election_trigger +]**, we bring the **[+
snap_campaign_strategy +]** campaign to the polling stations. The slogans,
alliances and party splits are over; voters now decide which of those parties
will return through the filed lists or district pacts.

- @poland_regional_campaign.snap_close: Make the closing regional choice

@snap_campaign_count
title: Count the ballots
go-to: snap_result_2026

@snap_defer
title: Wait for another legal trigger
subtitle: Keep the election request alive and review the count next month.
view-if: snap_election_requested = 1 and snap_budget_deadline_ready = 0
on-arrival: snap_event_deferred_time = time; public_trust -= 1; news_headline = "The election request remains pending while constitutional clocks run"
go-to: poland_event_queue

@snap_avoid
title: Withdraw the election demand and return to a minority budget bargain
subtitle: Preserve the present cabinet at the cost of an obvious retreat.
view-if: snap_election_requested = 1
on-arrival: snap_election_requested = 0; early_election_risk = 45; party_unity -= 4; ko_relation += 2; psl_relation += 3; public_trust -= 2; news_headline = "A minority bargain avoids immediate dissolution without changing who holds office"

PSL and KO take the reopened budget talks. Our own caucus must explain why an
election described as necessary yesterday can be traded away today.

- @poland_event_queue: Withdraw the demand

@snap_waive_deadline
title: Submit the case against shortening the term
subtitle: Lewica may argue for continuity, but the President still decides independently.
view-if: snap_election_requested = 0 and snap_budget_deadline_ready = 1
on-arrival: {!
Q.snap_election_trigger =
    "Article 225 review after the budget deadline";
Q.snap_budget_petition_advocacy = -8;
Q.news_headline =
    "Lewica asks the Palace not to shorten the term";
!}
go-to: snap_budget_palace_decision

@snap_formation_attempt_one
title: First formation attempt — the President's nominee
new-page: true
# Runs after this scene's own on-arrival, so the player's join option is
# judged on the relations this stage just moved.
call: poland_normalize
on-arrival: {!
const firstRight =
    Q.government_party == "pis" ||
    Q.president_name == "Andrzej Duda" ||
    Boolean(Q.pres_2025_hostile_president);
const successionNominee =
    Q.office_incompatibility_pm_formation &&
    String(Q.office_incompatibility_pm_nominee || "").length &&
    Q.office_incompatibility_pm_nominee != Q.president_name
        ? Q.office_incompatibility_pm_nominee
        : "";
const rightNominee = Q.president_name == "Mateusz Morawiecki"
    ? "Beata Szydło"
    : "Mateusz Morawiecki";
Q.snap_formation_candidate = successionNominee || (firstRight
    ? rightNominee
    : (
        String(Q.prime_minister || "").length &&
        !String(Q.prime_minister || "").includes("Vacant") &&
        Q.prime_minister != Q.president_name
            ? Q.prime_minister
            : (Q.ko_leader || "KO nominee")
    ));
const firstNomineeParty = successionNominee
    ? String(Q.office_incompatibility_pm_nominee_party || "")
    : "";
Q.snap_formation_first_right = successionNominee
    ? (firstNomineeParty == "pis" ? 1 : 0)
    : (firstRight ? 1 : 0);
Q.snap_formation_nominee_is_left =
    firstNomineeParty == "lewica" || [
        "Agnieszka Dziemianowicz-Bąk", "Magdalena Biejat",
        "Krzysztof Gawkowski", "Włodzimierz Czarzasty",
        "Robert Biedroń", "Adrian Zandberg"
    ].includes(Q.snap_formation_candidate) ? 1 : 0;
const sharedRightFormation = Math.max(
    0,
    Number(Q.snap_election_right_2027_seats) || 0
);
const pisKonfPledge = sharedRightFormation > 0
    ? Math.max(0, sharedRightFormation - Number(Q.pis_seats || 0))
    : (Q.coalition_viable_pis_konf &&
        (Number(Q.rival_relation_pis_konf) || 0) >= 50
        ? Math.max(0, Number(Q.konf_seats) || 0) +
            Math.max(0, Number(Q.new_hope_seats) || 0) +
            Math.max(0, Number(Q.national_movement_seats) || 0) +
            Math.max(0, Number(Q.korona_seats) || 0)
        : 0);
const pisPslPledge =
    Q.coalition_viable_pis_psl &&
    (Number(Q.rival_relation_pis_psl) || 0) >= 55 &&
    (Number(Q.psl_coalition_dissent) || 0) < 65
        ? Math.max(0, Number(Q.psl_seats) || 0)
        : 0;
const koPslPledge =
    Q.coalition_viable_ko_psl &&
    (Number(Q.rival_relation_ko_psl) || 0) >= 55 &&
    (Number(Q.psl_coalition_dissent) || 0) < 65
        ? Math.max(0, Number(Q.psl_seats) || 0)
        : 0;
const koP2050Pledge =
    Q.coalition_viable_ko_p2050 &&
    (Number(Q.rival_relation_ko_p2050) || 0) >= 55 &&
    (Number(Q.p2050_coalition_dissent) || 0) < 65
        ? Math.max(0, Number(Q.p2050_seats) || 0)
        : 0;
const centrumPledge =
    (Number(Q.centrum_relation) || 0) >= 55
        ? Math.max(0, Number(Q.centrum_seats) || 0)
        : 0;
Q.right_committed_seats =
    Math.max(0, Number(Q.pis_seats) || 0) + pisKonfPledge +
    (sharedRightFormation > 0
        ? Math.max(0, Number(Q.duda_seats) || 0) +
            Math.max(0, Number(Q.social_conservative_seats) || 0)
        : ((Number(Q.pis_relation) || 0) >= 45
            ? Math.max(0, Number(Q.rozwoj_seats) || 0) +
                Math.max(0, Number(Q.duda_seats) || 0) +
                Math.max(0, Number(Q.social_conservative_seats) || 0)
            : 0));
Q.democratic_committed_seats =
    Math.max(0, Number(Q.ko_seats) || 0) + koPslPledge +
    koP2050Pledge + centrumPledge;
Q.snap_psl_cabinet_committed = Q.snap_formation_first_right
    ? (pisPslPledge > 0 ? 1 : 0)
    : (koPslPledge > 0 ? 1 : 0);
Q.snap_p2050_cabinet_committed =
    !Q.snap_formation_first_right && koP2050Pledge > 0 ? 1 : 0;
Q.snap_centrum_cabinet_committed =
    !Q.snap_formation_first_right && centrumPledge > 0 ? 1 : 0;
Q.snap_left_cabinet_commitment = 0;
if (Q.snap_formation_first_right) {
    Q.snap_formation_base = Q.right_committed_seats + pisPslPledge;
    Q.snap_formation_pledge_basis =
        "PiS" + (pisKonfPledge ? " · Konfederacja pact" : "") +
        (pisPslPledge ? " · PSL pact" : "");
} else {
    Q.snap_formation_base = Q.democratic_committed_seats;
    Q.snap_formation_pledge_basis =
        "KO" + (koPslPledge ? " · PSL pact" : "") +
        (koP2050Pledge ? " · Poland 2050 pact" : "") +
        (centrumPledge ? " · Centrum pact" : "");
}
Q.snap_formation_base = Math.max(
    0,
    Math.min(460, Math.round(Q.snap_formation_base))
);
Q.snap_formation_left_votes = 0;
Q.news_headline =
    Q.president_name + " nominates " +
    Q.snap_formation_candidate + " in the first attempt";
!}

= An appointment still needs 231

The nominee begins with **[+ snap_formation_base +]** expected votes from **[+
snap_formation_pledge_basis +]**. Other parties are possible partners, not
automatic yes votes; Lewica controls
only its own **[+ left_committed_seats +]** committed votes.

- @snap_attempt_one_support
- @snap_attempt_one_join
- @snap_attempt_one_reject

@snap_attempt_one_support
title: Supply confidence for a time-limited constitutional cabinet
view-if: snap_formation_nominee_is_left = 0
on-arrival: snap_formation_left_votes = left_committed_seats; snap_left_cabinet_commitment = 0; party_unity -= 5; public_trust -= 1; pis_relation += 5 if snap_formation_first_right = 1; ko_relation += 3 if snap_formation_first_right = 0; news_headline = "Lewica offers confidence without claiming to control the nominee"
go-to: snap_attempt_one_vote

@snap_attempt_one_join
title: Join a non-hostile nominee under a written cabinet agreement
subtitle: Confidence entails real collective responsibility and ministries.
view-if: snap_formation_first_right = 0
choose-if: coalition_viable_left_ko = 1
unavailable-subtitle: KO and Lewica are too far apart, in trust and in programme, to sign a cabinet agreement; confidence from outside is still on offer.
on-arrival: snap_formation_left_votes = left_committed_seats; snap_left_cabinet_commitment = 1; party_unity += 1; ko_relation += 3; government_coalition_dissent += 2; news_headline = "Lewica joins the first-attempt cabinet under a written programme"
go-to: snap_attempt_one_vote

@snap_attempt_one_reject
title: Reject the presidential nominee
on-arrival: snap_formation_left_votes = 0; party_unity += 2; pis_relation -= 3 if snap_formation_first_right = 1; news_headline = "Lewica withholds confidence from the first attempt"
go-to: snap_attempt_one_vote

@snap_attempt_one_vote
title: First-attempt confidence vote
new-page: true
on-arrival: {!
const attemptOneRoll =
    Math.floor((this.random.uint32() / 4294967296) * 7) - 3;
Q.snap_formation_variance = attemptOneRoll;
Q.confidence_candidate = Q.snap_formation_candidate;
Q.confidence_yes = Math.max(
    0,
    Math.min(
        460,
        Q.snap_formation_base +
        (Number(Q.snap_formation_left_votes) || 0) +
        attemptOneRoll
    )
);
Q.confidence_abstain = Math.max(
    0,
    Math.min(24, 460 - Q.confidence_yes)
);
Q.confidence_no = Math.max(
    0,
    460 - Q.confidence_yes - Q.confidence_abstain
);
Q.confidence_present = 460;
Q.confidence_threshold = 231;
Q.government_has_confidence =
    Q.confidence_yes >= 231 ? 1 : 0;
Q.snap_formation_attempt = 1;
!}

**[+ confidence_yes +] yes · [+ confidence_no +] no · [+
confidence_abstain +] abstain.** The first attempt requires 231 yes votes.

- @snap_formation_success
- @snap_formation_attempt_two

@snap_formation_attempt_two
title: Second formation attempt — the Sejm's nominee
new-page: true
view-if: government_has_confidence = 0
call: poland_normalize
on-arrival: {!
const leftCandidate =
    (Number(Q.ko_relation) || 0) < 34 &&
    (Number(Q.left_committed_seats) || 0) >= 45;
const eligibleLeftNominees = [
    Q.pres_2025_left_candidate,
    "Agnieszka Dziemianowicz-Bąk",
    "Magdalena Biejat",
    "Krzysztof Gawkowski",
    "Katarzyna Kotula"
].filter(function(name) {
    return name && name != "Undecided" && name != Q.president_name;
});
Q.snap_formation_candidate = leftCandidate
    ? eligibleLeftNominees[0]
    : (
        Q.president_name == Q.ko_leader
            ? Q.snap_progressive_ko_candidate
            : (Q.ko_leader || "KO nominee")
    );
Q.snap_formation_nominee_is_left = leftCandidate ? 1 : 0;
const sejmKoPslPledge =
    Q.coalition_viable_ko_psl &&
    (Number(Q.rival_relation_ko_psl) || 0) >= 55 &&
    (Number(Q.psl_coalition_dissent) || 0) < 65
        ? Math.max(0, Number(Q.psl_seats) || 0)
        : 0;
const sejmKoP2050Pledge =
    Q.coalition_viable_ko_p2050 &&
    (Number(Q.rival_relation_ko_p2050) || 0) >= 55 &&
    (Number(Q.p2050_coalition_dissent) || 0) < 65
        ? Math.max(0, Number(Q.p2050_seats) || 0)
        : 0;
const sejmCentrumPledge =
    (Number(Q.centrum_relation) || 0) >= 55
        ? Math.max(0, Number(Q.centrum_seats) || 0)
        : 0;
Q.democratic_committed_seats =
    Math.max(0, Number(Q.ko_seats) || 0) + sejmKoPslPledge +
    sejmKoP2050Pledge + sejmCentrumPledge;
Q.snap_psl_cabinet_committed = sejmKoPslPledge > 0 ? 1 : 0;
Q.snap_p2050_cabinet_committed = sejmKoP2050Pledge > 0 ? 1 : 0;
Q.snap_centrum_cabinet_committed = sejmCentrumPledge > 0 ? 1 : 0;
Q.snap_left_cabinet_commitment = 0;
Q.snap_formation_base = Q.democratic_committed_seats;
Q.snap_formation_pledge_basis =
    "KO" + (sejmKoPslPledge ? " · PSL pact" : "") +
    (sejmKoP2050Pledge ? " · Poland 2050 pact" : "") +
    (sejmCentrumPledge ? " · Centrum pact" : "");
if (leftCandidate) {
    Q.snap_formation_base -= Math.round(
        Math.max(0, Number(Q.ko_seats) || 0) * 0.16
    );
}
Q.snap_formation_base = Math.max(
    0,
    Math.min(460, Math.round(Q.snap_formation_base))
);
Q.snap_formation_left_votes = 0;
Q.news_headline =
    "The Sejm proposes " + Q.snap_formation_candidate +
    " in the second attempt";
!}

The Sejm nominee begins with **[+ snap_formation_base +]** votes from **[+
snap_formation_pledge_basis +]** before Lewica commits its caucus. This stage
also requires an absolute majority of 231.

- @snap_attempt_two_support
- @snap_attempt_two_join
- @snap_attempt_two_reject

